Description: adapt BeEncoder to the media2 track and format API
 media2 keeps BMediaFile/BMediaTrack and the legacy names, but the track
 format calls take BMediaFormat (a wrapper whose public media_format member
 is assigned in and out) instead of media_format*, and media_file_format
 knows only B_KNOWS_RAW_VIDEO/B_KNOWS_RAW_AUDIO/B_KNOWS_OTHER - there is no
 B_KNOWS_ENCODED_VIDEO to test. The three track calls now round-trip
 through a BMediaFormat, and the encoder menu filter keeps the raw-video
 test alone (the encoded-video test could never compile; on V\OS the
 format list comes from the GStreamer-backed media_file_format enumeration
 where video-remux containers simply do not carry a raw-video capability).
Author: Numerio <b.vitruvio@gmail.com>
Forwarded: no
Origin: https://github.com/HaikuArchives/Hare

